00:05:22.065 --> 00:05:24.700
Next,

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:30.080
I will give you some time.  Do you remember what this is about?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.240
The quote in lam rim is tsul trim den pay ge long ud dang den (TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN)

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.560
Someone who truly keeps their vows,

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.720
truly keeps their Buddhist guidelines, especially the 10 guidelines,

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.620
they shine, truly shine.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:58.656
A person who makes a healthy, humble effort to keep their commitments,

00:05:58.656 --> 00:06:01.360
to maintain the ten good karma and

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.000
be kind to others,

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.519
they have a kind of peaceful look on their face,

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.160
they glow.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.260
When they walk into a room, you know it.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:17.360
Everyone started to feel better, like Tim and Seiji.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.860
It is the light of the world.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.240
Buddha said, those people are the light of the world.

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.380
There are Christian expressions;

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:32.400
Don't put candles in a basket, let the world see your happy face.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:39.960
And it is a true guiding light for the whole world.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.440
Next image IDIM #4

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:57.600
This is the cliff I visited with my partner Veronica on her birthday, during this lam rim.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:06.940
They talk about sunset, for which the Tibetan word is nub pa (NUB PA).

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:10.580
It also means west because the sun sets in the west;

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.500
nub pa means

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:16.080
sunset and it is a very sad verb.

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:20.820
This is a very sad idea in dharma, The

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:27.980
most famous place at the end of Abhidharmakosha;  Treasure House of Higher Wisdom.  The

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:31.760
Treasure House of Higher Knowledge by Master Vasabhandu, and he says;

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:39.060
"the sun of dharma, the light of dharma, will set in this world."

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:43.440
We will lose the light of dharma in this world.  This world will plunge into darkness.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.520
After some time,

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.560
Buddhism will disappear in this world.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:56.060
At first they disappeared from people's minds, but they still exist in libraries.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:59.600
The books are still in the library.  Maybe a library that John Brady hasn't discovered yet.

00:08:00.319 --> 00:08:04.239
And then, they'll disappear from the library too and then they'll be gone forever.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:11.840
I put the picture here because Pabongka Rinpoche made a special point, he said:

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:19.520
'if you cannot keep your commitments, if you cannot be kind to others,

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:22.640
then we can say the dharma has left this world.'

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:26.319
The light of dharma has left the world within you.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.780
The sun has set within your own chest,

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:34.460
which would be a very sad thing if we did not keep our promise.

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:36.560
Next image.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:48.200
We call this retreat Love in the Time of Virus.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:55.440
The bottom line is that during a very difficult time in the world,

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.600
if you keep your commitments,

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.860
if you are kind to others,

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.320
when things are scary, and the virus is spreading.

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.160
We don't know where, we don't know how, and

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.880
we don't know how many people will die.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:16.660
If during difficult times you do something kind for others,

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.160
this is much, much more powerful.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:22.420
He mentioned, if you remember, a 5-star Buddhist paradise,

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.759
which is like the perfect place.

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:29.839
It's easy to be a good person, everyone there is a good person.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:33.236
That's not a big achievement.                                            It's not a big deal,

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:35.220
and the seeds aren't strong enough

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.580
to be nice in a group of nice people.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:42.880
To be kind when people attack you, when people are afraid,

00:09:43.839 --> 00:09:47.518
when people are not kind to each other and to be someone

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:54.060
who stands up and shares things in difficult times -

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.340
then that is a very pure person.

00:09:57.520 --> 00:10:01.500
That's great karma.  That's incredible karma, much more powerful.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.840
I think this virus is a very good time, and

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:09.120
it is a very good opportunity for all of us to show

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:14.380
- are we really Buddhist?   Are we truly practicing the bodhisattva path?

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.560
Can we help others even when things are very difficult.

