Next picture #7

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:23.300
Try to remember what this picture is about?  I'll give it a moment.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:31.680
This is my favorite topic;

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:42.000
have a personal relationship with another person, like these two people.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:47.866
In my opinion and in tantra, it is one of the happiest things that can happen to you.

00:12:47.866 --> 00:12:51.860
It's one of the greatest things that can happen to you.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:57.520
Anyone will tell you the reason the whole world is looking for a partner,

00:12:58.399 --> 00:13:00.082
is to make people happy.

00:13:00.082 --> 00:13:03.279
It is one of the greatest joys when things go well.

00:13:04.399 --> 00:13:07.518
It's one of the greatest joys you can have but

00:13:08.399 --> 00:13:12.799
you know and I know when it doesn't go well,

00:13:13.519 --> 00:13:16.159
it's one of the greatest pains in life.

00:13:16.959 --> 00:13:19.839
Why is it relevant to this lesson?

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:29.120
If your morality is good,

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:31.360
this is the happiest thing in your life.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:37.040
And if you violate your morality, it is also the same thing that will make you miserable.

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:40.320
It's like having a good woman or man, who is your partner, the

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.620
same person who makes you really happy,

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:47.860
can also make you really miserable.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:52.400
So in this case, the vinaya, your personal practice of goodness,

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:56.240
good behavior, compared to a partner

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:59.540
who can make you the best thing in life

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.320
or the worst thing in your life - the same person.

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:10.120
IDIM next #8

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.840
This one is tricky.  See if you remember?

00:14:15.519 --> 00:14:17.519
I'll take a sip of my green drink.

00:14:18.639 --> 00:14:20.639
Thank you Vimala.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:33.560
This actually symbolizes breaking your commitment.  Pulling weeds

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.720
represents breaking your commitments.

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:45.260
Why would destroying this plant violate your commitment?

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:51.560
If you are a gardener you know that you have to pull the weeds out

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:54.640
before the seeds are ready to burst.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:59.380
If you wait until the seedlings are ready to emerge and then

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.920
start pulling the plants out,

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:04.560
you will end up spreading about a thousand seedlings.

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:11.260
For the next month or next year you will have thousands of weeds growing back.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.440
So you have to attack the weeds early.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:19.140
This refers to a very radical statement

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.360
that Buddha said

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:27.900
ge long dak sok dang drel shing shi wa ni lay (DGE SLONG DAG SROG DANG BRAL ZHING SHI BA NI BLA'I) It is

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.240
better to die

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.479
than to break your vows.  Why?

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.680
When you break a vow,

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.980
you sow a seed

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:42.660
that will continue to grow for many lifetimes.

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:49.740
If you die you destroy one mind body complex.

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:54.060
If you die, you destroy a very useful temple,

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:57.360
a temple of the physical and the mind.  You lost one.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.560
But if you break the commitment,

00:16:01.279 --> 00:16:04.440
you lose a lot of mind-body complexes.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.458
You damage your body and mind for many lifetimes.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:11.440
And you create a moving seed

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.280
that will destroy many lives.

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:20.420
Buddha said, it is better to die than to break a vow and

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:27.460
that is not a metaphor.  He was being very literal

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:31.280
when he said that.  Better to die than break your commitment.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:35.360
There is a joke in the lamrim.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:44.320
We vow never to give up bodhichitta even at the cost of our lives.

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:52.480
There is a famous saying, all our life we ​​are waiting

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.720
to be put in jail

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.880
by some bad people.

00:16:57.199 --> 00:17:02.479
They came with knives and they said 'give up your bodhisattva vows or die today'.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.799
Then we will say;

00:17:04.799 --> 00:17:06.480
'I choose to die'.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:09.199
And they kill us.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.280
I think we've all been waiting for this moment since we took that oath.

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:18.300
We're all waiting for these guys to show up with knives and threaten us.

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:22.960
But actually we are the ones with the knives.  We threaten our own bodhisattva vows every day.

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:31.840
We must make this decision every day when we decide to keep our vows carefully.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.860
It's hard to find the people who put you in jail, and say;

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:41.440
I will kill you if you don't hand over your bodhisattva vows.

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.720
Next image.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:54.540
See if you remember.  I'll give you some time to try to remember it.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:05.840
This is a reference....

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:09.039
we have a Mixed Nuts translation team

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:12.559
and we are translating the old vinaya texts;

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:16.440
monastic vows, nun's vows.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:25.140
They talk about vows, traditions that we are not supposed to...

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:29.820
...when you become a monk or a nun they give you robes,

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.840
they give you a small buddha statue,

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.960
and they give you a sieve.

00:18:35.919 --> 00:18:39.279
And in ancient India you were supposed to carry this sieve with you.

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:43.360
When you drink from the river,

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:49.439
you should filter the water first to make sure you don't kill any small insects.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:55.680
We mentioned a well-known tradition in the vinaya:

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:59.200
if two monks go to the river to drink water

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:02.380
to get some water,

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:07.340
then they must choose the best monk to check the water.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:15.040
Don't choose someone who doesn't care about insects.  Try to find a guy who loves bugs

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:19.280
and have them check the water because they will be more careful.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:22.000
What is the point?

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:26.440
We're talking about a kind of ecological vow,

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:31.540
where monks and nuns aren't even supposed to pick green leaves

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:37.560
from plants because they're the homes of tiny creatures.

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:43.000
This means, honoring even the smallest vows,

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:49.180
keeping them very seriously because the results are multiplied.

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:53.600
Then, it is important to maintain your morality at a very subtle level,

00:19:55.039 --> 00:19:58.399
at a very subtle level.

00:20:00.559 --> 00:20:02.549
If I were to write a bodhisattva vow,

00:20:02.549 --> 00:20:04.719
I would write an extra bodhisattva vow about

00:20:05.039 --> 00:20:07.199
not offending your bodhisattva vow.

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:09.840
There's nothing more annoying than

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:14.420
someone telling you that they kept their oath and

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:17.760
that's why they have to be an asshole today.

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:23.199
Keep your vows sweet.  Keep them happy.  Do not exaggerate.

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:29.760
Don't bother others with your swearing because your swearing doesn't bother others.

00:20:30.559 --> 00:20:35.279
Keeping small vows, keeping them quietly.  Keep them private, don't advertise.

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:42.159
There is a saying in Islam... the left hand should not let the right hand know what it is doing.

00:20:43.039 --> 00:20:46.799
That means, don't advertise your vows.  Just keep them quiet.

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:49.840
Keeping them at a very subtle level.

00:20:50.559 --> 00:20:52.559
