This is about pride.

00:29:13.279 --> 00:29:16.398
Pride will also be an obstacle to keeping your vows.

00:29:17.279 --> 00:29:20.799
And... one of the most common types of pride

00:29:21.520 --> 00:29:26.540
in the monastic context, where this book is commonly taught;

00:29:28.960 --> 00:29:33.920
is how much you know about ancient scriptures, how many facts you have collected

00:29:34.560 --> 00:29:35.780
in life.

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:39.920
This is something I really enjoy, about the understanding of dharma

00:29:39.920 --> 00:29:41.760
and the more you collect

00:29:42.100 --> 00:29:45.760
the more special you feel.

00:29:46.559 --> 00:29:51.487
Pabongka Rinpoche said, 'All the dharma you've ever studied in your life, all the things you've memorized,

00:29:51.487 --> 00:29:53.300
all the things you've debated,

00:29:53.300 --> 00:29:55.360
all the geshe titles you've ever had,

00:29:57.100 --> 00:30:02.820
compared to what's left to know, you know nothing.

00:30:03.100 --> 00:30:06.160
You are like a worm at the bottom of the sea,

00:30:06.880 --> 00:30:08.799
and sometimes you come out and look at the stars.

00:30:11.520 --> 00:30:14.239
Many stars have planets around them.

00:30:15.120 --> 00:30:19.039
There are people on those planets.  There are things to know about those people.

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:23.100
There are things we know,

00:30:23.280 --> 00:30:25.280
that we are so proud of,

00:30:26.240 --> 00:30:32.420
that are a small fraction of what you can know.

00:30:33.820 --> 00:30:35.840
So don't be arrogant.

00:30:35.840 --> 00:30:37.840
Next.

